From bea0ec2c5767c0315fd854639ae3b7ef832ff323 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hyunW3 <0176778602@naver.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 16:37:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 14/22] b200: enable torch.compile (~1.7x) +
 training/eval/monitor helpers

torch.compile works on B200/sm_100 after ENABLE_INTRA_NODE_COMM=0 (the real
get_group_info root cause, status.md crash7), validated via 20-step smoke tests
on both the llama (SDPA) and AU-Net (xformers-fmha) paths. Compiled iter ~0.41s
vs 0.68s uncompiled for llama (~1.7x); ~1.6x for AU-Net.

- llama_1B_b200.yaml / aunet2_1.3B_b200.yaml: compile=true; refresh stale
  get_group_info / SAC / batch-size comments
- apps/main/train.py: manual DTensor-safe clip (mirrors apps/aunet) so the
  traced full_tensor() collective isn't hit under compile
- train_llama_1B.sh / train_aunet.sh: 4-GPU torchrun + TMPDIR=/var/tmp
  (/tmp is noexec -> compiled .so fails to mmap; long lustre path overflows the
  AF_UNIX socket limit); drop invalid ckpt_dir= arg (lingua auto-resumes)
- run_eval_llama.sh + eval_llama_1B_b200.yaml: downstream eval (HellaSwag/ARC-E)
- monitor_llama_milestones.sh: Telegram alerts at 30/60/100% + auto-eval
- *_compile_smoke.yaml: short compile smoke-test configs
- status.md: add TMPDIR to documented launch commands

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
